  "important_notes": [
    "Do not treat a poll's vote-share estimate as a probability of victory unless the source explicitly publishes a probability model.",
    "Use the final poll before each election for the cleanest pollster-vs-result comparison; keep all polls separately for trend/house-effect analyses.",
    "Do not infer bias/manipulation from who commissioned a poll. Keep commissioner as a variable and test empirically.",
    "TSE PesqEle public polling datasets start in 2012, so Brazilian 2010 poll values require separate historical/manual sourcing.",
    "Europepolls is a secondary aggregator whose raw data was mined from Wikipedia; validate final selected rows against original pollster publications.",
    "For US national presidential polls compare against national popular-vote share, not Electoral College winner.",
    "For Brazil 2026, use TSE 2026 as the registry backbone and pollster releases for actual candidate percentages."
  ]
